AdamW compute and H100 time
  AdamW FLOPs per parameter
    weight decay     mul + sub = 2  # theta <- theta - lr * wd * theta
    m update         2 mul + add = 3  # m <- beta1*m + (1-beta1)*g
    v update         square + 2 mul + add = 4  # v <- beta2*v + (1-beta2)*g^2
    Adam update      sqrt + add + div + mul + sub = 5  # theta update with m/sqrt(v)
  AdamW optimizer FLOPs:     ~14 FLOPs/parameter = 22.90B FLOPs per optimizer step
  forward FLOPs / sequence: 3.51T
  training step uses forward + backward, and backward is assumed to be 2x forward.
  with batch_size=1024: 1024 * 3 * 3.51T + 22.90B
  train step FLOPs:         batch_size * 3 * forward + AdamW = 10,772.62T (10.77P)
  H100 effective FLOPs/s:   247.50T FLOP/s at 50% MFU
  400,000 steps, batch=1024: 4836.19 hours
